"display-unstructured">Lempp H, Seale C. The hidden curriculum in undergraduate medical education: qualitative study of medical students&#x02019; perceptions of teaching. BMJ. 2004;329:770&#x02013;3. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15459051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sheehan</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sheehan</surname><given-names>DV</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Leibowitz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Baldwin</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A pilot study of medical student &#x0201c;abuse&#x0201d;: student perceptions of mistreatment and misconduct in medical school</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>1990</year><volume>263</volume><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>537</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.263.4.533</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Sheehan KH, Sheehan DV, White K, Leibowitz A, Baldwin DC. A pilot study of medical student &#x0201c;abuse&#x0201d;: student perceptions of mistreatment and misconduct in medical school. JAMA. 1990;263:533&#x02013;7. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2294325</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baldwin</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Daugherty</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Eckenfels</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Student perceptions of mistreatment and harassment during medical school: a survey of ten United States schools</article-title><source>West J Med</source><year>1991</year><volume>155</volume><fpage>140</fpage><lpage>145</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Baldw